    <briefdescription>
<para>Timing middleware that logs how long a request took to produce its response. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Part of both the INSECURE and SECURE chains. It records a steady_clock start, passes the request onward, and measures the interval in the return-path callback when the downstream handler&apos;s response propagates back out. The result is logged with request IP, method, status and path; the response is then forwarded unchanged. Stateless and safe for concurrent requests: all per-request state lives in the callback capture. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
